METRICA is a from-scratch successor of "Sopralluogo" (https://github.com/gabrielevierti/sopralluogo,
MIT License). No source code of Sopralluogo is included; some of its ideas (people as a ruler for
single-view calibration, background plates, planar snapping, honest labelling of inferred content)
were re-implemented.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Model weights
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
No model weights are distributed with METRICA. They are downloaded by the user from their original
publishers under their own licences, listed in docs/MODEL_LICENSES.md.

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Python dependencies
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Python dependencies are installed by the user from PyPI and are not redistributed in the METRICA
source or release archive. Their licences are listed in docs/MODEL_LICENSES.md. Note that the PyAV
binary wheels bundle FFmpeg libraries built with GPL components (libx264, libx265).

